+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_Kg0B5iSyKdDcJUhzPHyF6788","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have now read every single file in the project. Here is my comprehensive report.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Directory Layout\n\n```\n/workspace/\n  .eslintrc.cjs              -- ESLint config (CommonJS, 428 bytes)\n  .gitignore                 -- Ignores: node_modules/, dist/\n  .thunderdome/\n    rubric.yaml              -- Scoring rubric for the T9 benchmark\n  .thunderdome-output.jsonl  -- Session log (previous agent actions)\n  .thunderdome-stderr.log    -- Empty\n  TASK.md                    -- Task instructions (building 8 plugins)\n  package.json               -- Project manifest\n  package-lock.json          -- Lockfile (138 KB)\n  tsconfig.json              -- TypeScript compiler config\n  vitest.config.ts           -- Vitest config\n\n  src/\n    core/\n      types.ts               -- Core type definitions (Plugin interface, etc.)\n      engine.ts              -- BuildEngine class (plugin orchestrator)\n      templates.ts           -- Default and list templates\n      index.ts               -- Barrel re-export file\n    plugins/\n      .gitkeep               -- Empty placeholder (plugins go here)\n\n  tests/\n    core.test.ts             -- 15 existing tests for BuildEngine\n    plugins/\n      asset-pipeline.test.ts -- 7 tests\n      dev-server.test.ts     -- 6 tests\n      markdown-ext.test.ts   -- 8 tests\n      rss-feed.test.ts       -- 8 tests\n      search-index.test.ts   -- 8 tests\n      sitemap.test.ts        -- 7 tests\n      syntax-highlight.test.ts -- 8 tests\n      taxonomy.test.ts       -- 8 tests\n```\n\nTotal: 60 new test cases across 8 plugin test files, plus 15 existing core tests = 75 total.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Full Contents of `/workspace/src/core/types.ts`\n\nThis file defines the complete type system for the SSG toolkit. It contains 5 interfaces:\n\n- **`SiteConfig`** -- project configuration (title, baseUrl, outputDir, contentDir, templateDir)\n- **`ContentFile`** -- a content page (slug, title, content, metadata, optional date/tags/template)\n- **`BuildContext`** -- the context passed through the build pipeline (config, files, output Map<string, string>, assets Map<string, Buffer>, data Map<string, unknown>)\n- **`PluginHooks`** -- three optional lifecycle hooks: `beforeBuild`, `transformContent`, `afterBuild`\n- **`Plugin`** -- the plugin shape: `name`, `version`, `dependencies` (string[]), `hooks` (PluginHooks)\n- **`Template`** -- a template with a `name` and a `render(content, data)` function\n\nKey detail: `transformContent` receives a single `ContentFile` and the `BuildContext`, and returns either `ContentFile` or `Promise<ContentFile>`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Full Contents of `/workspace/src/core/` (the SSG Toolkit)\n\n### `/workspace/src/core/engine.ts` -- `BuildEngine` class\n\n- Maintains a private `plugins` array and `templates` Map\n- `registerPlugin(plugin)` -- pushes to the plugins array\n- `registerTemplate(template)` -- stores by name in the Map\n- `resolvePluginOrder()` -- performs a **topological sort** on plugins based on their `dependencies` arrays. Throws on circular dependencies (`visiting` set detects cycles) and missing dependencies (checks `pluginMap.has(dep)`)\n- `build(files)` -- the main build pipeline:\n  1. Creates a `BuildContext` with a copy of files, empty output/assets/data Maps\n  2. Calls all `beforeBuild` hooks in topological order (awaits if Promise)\n  3. Calls all `transformContent` hooks in topological order -- each plugin processes every file, and the results replace `ctx.files`\n  4. **Template rendering**: for each file, looks up the template by `file.template` (defaults to `'default'`), calls `template.render(file.content, data)` where data includes title/slug/date/tags/metadata/siteTitle/baseUrl, stores result in `ctx.output` at `{slug}.html`. Falls back to raw content if no template found.\n  5. Calls all `afterBuild` hooks in topological order\n  6. Returns the `BuildContext`\n- `getPlugins()` -- returns a copy of the plugins array\n- `getTemplates()` -- returns a copy of the templates Map\n\n### `/workspace/src/core/templates.ts` -- Template factories\n\n- `createDefaultTemplate()` -- returns a `Template` named `'default'` that renders a full HTML5 document with `<article>`, `<h1>`, optional `<time>`, and `<div class=\"content\">`\n- `createListTemplate()` -- returns a `Template` named `'list'` that renders a simpler page with `<div class=\"list\">`\n\n### `/workspace/src/core/index.ts` -- Barrel file\n\nRe-exports everything: `BuildEngine`, `createDefaultTemplate`, `createListTemplate`, and all types.\n\n---\n\n## 4. All Test Files -- What They Test\n\n### `/workspace/tests/core.test.ts` (15 tests -- must continue to pass)\n\nThese test the `BuildEngine` core:\n1. `registers plugins` -- verifies `getPlugins()` returns the registered plugin\n2. `registers templates` -- verifies `getTemplates().has('default')`\n3. `builds with default template and renders HTML` -- checks DOCTYPE, title, content, site title in output\n4. `builds with list template and renders list HTML` -- checks `<div class=\"list\">`\n5. `outputs raw content when no matching template` -- when template name not registered, raw content is used\n6. `calls plugin beforeBuild hook` -- sets a flag, verifies it was called\n7. `calls plugin transformContent hook to transform files` -- uppercases content, checks result\n8. `calls plugin afterBuild hook` -- sets a flag, verifies it was called\n9. `executes plugins in dependency order` -- verifies topological sort (b depends on a, so order is a, b)\n10. `throws on circular dependency` -- a->b, b->a\n11. `throws on missing dependency` -- a depends on 'missing', which is not registered\n12. `applies multiple plugins transformContent in order` -- chained appending, verifies `'start [first] [second]'`\n13. `provides shared data store in build context` -- sets data in beforeBuild, reads it after\n14. `retains file metadata through build` -- verifies metadata/date/tags survive build\n15. `produces empty output for empty file list` -- empty files array yields empty output\n\n### `/workspace/tests/plugins/asset-pipeline.test.ts` (7 tests)\n\nPlugin: `createAssetPipelinePlugin()` -- implemented in `src/plugins/asset-pipeline.js`\n\nTests:\n1. Rewrites relative image URLs (`./image.png` -> `/assets/image.png`)\n2. Rewrites relative link URLs (`./doc.pdf` -> `/assets/doc.pdf`)\n3. Leaves absolute URLs unchanged (`https://cdn.example.com/...`)\n4. Generates asset manifest in `ctx.data` with key `'asset-manifest'` (object with `assets: string[]`)\n5. Handles files with no asset references (unchanged)\n6. Handles multiple assets in one file (all appear in manifest)\n7. Asset manifest includes all discovered assets across multiple files\n8. Does not double-process already-rewritten URLs (`/assets/...` left alone, not added to manifest)\n\n### `/workspace/tests/plugins/dev-server.test.ts` (6 tests)\n\nPlugin: `createDevServerPlugin()` -- implemented in `src/plugins/dev-server.js`\n\nTests:\n1. Stores `'dev-server-config'` in `ctx.data`\n2. Config includes a `port` (number)\n3. Config includes asset routes from `'asset-manifest'` data -- reads from `ctx.data` which would be populated by asset-pipeline. `assetPaths` contains asset filenames, `routes` includes entries with `handler: 'asset'`\n4. Config includes `searchIndexPath` (from `ctx.output` detecting `'search-index.json'`, expecting `/search-index.json`)\n5. Config includes content routes (`handler: 'static'`) for each HTML file in `ctx.output`\n6. Default port is 3000\n7. Handles missing `'asset-pipeline'` data gracefully (`assetPaths` equals `[]`)\n\n### `/workspace/tests/plugins/markdown-ext.test.ts` (8 tests)\n\nPlugin: `createMarkdownExtPlugin()` -- implemented in `src/plugins/markdown-ext.js`\n\nTests:\n1. Converts basic markdown to HTML (`# Hello`, `**bold**`)\n2. Handles footnotes with `[^1]` syntax (expects `<sup><a href=\"#fn-1\">1</a></sup>`)\n3. Renders footnote section at bottom (`<section class=\"footnotes\">` with `<li id=\"fn-1\">`)\n4. Converts `:::note` container to `<div class=\"admonition admonition-note\">`\n5. Converts `:::warning` container to admonition div\n6. Converts `:::tip` container to admonition div\n7. Preserves existing HTML content\n8. Handles empty content\n\n### `/workspace/tests/plugins/rss-feed.test.ts` (8 tests)\n\nPlugin: `createRssFeedPlugin()` -- implemented in `src/plugins/rss-feed.js`\n\nTests:\n1. Generates valid RSS 2.0 XML (`<?xml version=\"1.0\"`, `<rss version=\"2.0\">`, `<channel>`, `<item>`, `</rss>`)\n2. Feed items contain HTML content wrapped in CDATA (`<![CDATA[<p>...</p>]]>`)\n3. Feed items include `<category>` tags from the file's `tags` array, using taxonomy data (`ctx.data` key `'taxonomy-tags'`)\n4. Feed includes `<title>` channel title from config (`Test Site`)\n5. Feed items sorted by date newest first (string position check)\n6. Handles files without dates (no `<pubDate>undefined</pubDate>`)\n7. Feed link uses `baseUrl` from config (`https://example.com`, `https://example.com/post-1.html`)\n\n### `/workspace/tests/plugins/search-index.test.ts` (8 tests)\n\nPlugin: `createSearchIndexPlugin()` -- implemented in `src/plugins/search-index.js`\n\nTests:\n1. Generates `'search-index.json'` in `ctx.output`\n2. Index entries have `slug`, `title`, and `content` (plain text, stripped of HTML)\n3. HTML tags stripped from indexed content (no `<` or `>` characters)\n4. Code blocks included in searchable text (`const x = 1;`)\n5. Handles empty file list (returns `[]`)\n6. Search index is valid JSON (all entries, correct count)\n7. Index entries include `tags` array if present\n\n### `/workspace/tests/plugins/sitemap.test.ts` (7 tests)\n\nPlugin: `createSitemapPlugin()` -- implemented in `src/plugins/sitemap.js`\n\nTests:\n1. Generates `'sitemap.xml'` in `ctx.output`\n2. Includes all content page URLs (